# Oura

Nocturne can import sleep, heart rate and steps from an Oura ring. The data comes from the data
export that Oura gives every account. You do not need an Oura membership, and Nocturne does not
connect to your Oura account.

## Importing your Oura data

1. Sign in at [membership.ouraring.com/data-export](https://membership.ouraring.com/data-export)
   and request a data export. Oura can take some hours to prepare it.
2. When the export is ready, download the ZIP file. Do not unpack it.
3. In Nocturne, open **Site settings > Connectors & Apps** and choose **Oura**.
4. Select the ZIP file and click **Import**.

Nocturne shows how many sleep sessions, heart rate readings and days of steps it imported.

<Callout type="info" title="The import is not automatic">

  Nocturne has the data that was in the export when Oura made it. To add newer data, request a
  new export and import it. Nocturne updates the records that it already has, so the same night
  is not imported two times.

</Callout>

## What Nocturne imports

| Data | From the export |
| --- | --- |
| Sleep | Each sleep period with its sleep stages, heart rate and heart rate variability, and the daily sleep score and blood oxygen average |
| Heart rate | Each heart rate reading, day and night |
| Steps | The step total for each day |

If the export has two heart rate readings for the same instant, Nocturne keeps one.

Nocturne does not import the readiness score, the activity score, skin temperature, stress,
workouts or tags.

The largest file that Nocturne accepts is 40 MB.

## Deleting imported data

Open **Oura** in **Connectors & Apps** and use the delete option at the bottom of the page. This
removes the data that came from Oura exports. Your data at Oura does not change.
